# The biggest architectural issue

There are currently **two FinalBuilds architectures living in the repo**.

Old architecture:

```text
Entity
REL
generic property types
JSONL canonical
```

New architecture:

```text
typed nodes
typed relationships
R2 canonical events
native Hydra
```

The latest code follows the newer typed-node approach, although Hydra limitations have forced it to abandon meaningful edges.

You should kill this documentation ambiguity now.

There should be **one canonical architecture document**.

Everything else should explicitly say:

```text
SUPERSEDED BY:
FOUNDRY_ARCHITECTURE_vX
```

This matters enormously once agents start reading these docs as instructions.

